---
title: "liquidate_as_coin (Pebble Protocol: Lending Entry Points)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_pre_check: pre_liquidation_check(app, cap, market, liquidation_perm)
    q_pre_check --> q_timestamp: now = clock.timestamp_ms() / 1000
    q_timestamp --> q_get_repay: repay_amount = available_repay_coin.value()
    q_get_repay --> q_handle_liq: handle_liquidation(obligation_id, repay_coin, registry, oracle, clock, now, ctx)
    q_handle_liq --> q_post_liq: post_liquidation(now, repay_amount, ...)
    q_post_liq --> [*]: return (collateral_coin, refund_coin)

    note right of q_pre_check
        INV-001: caller must have liquidation permission (whitelist)
        INV-002: version must match
        INV-003: market must be validated
        INV-004: circuit break must not be triggered
    end note

    note right of q_handle_liq
        INV-005: repay_coin value must be non-zero
        INV-006: obligation must belong to this market
        INV-007: collateral asset must have can_be_collateral = true
        INV-008: liquidation must not be paused for collateral asset
        INV-009: obligation must be unsafe (weighted_debts > weighted_collateral)
        INV-010: close_factor enforced unless near bad debt
        INV-011: seized cTokens <= obligation total cTokens for that collateral
        INV-012: liquidation_revenue_factor portion goes to protocol reserve
    end note
